.TH "ODIR-DOT-JOBSTATUS" "7" "" "odir 25.1.2+onesimus.0.2.0" "Onesimus Director Commands"
.SH NAME
odir\-dot\-jobstatus \- \&.jobstatus: List jobstatus information
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&.jobstatus[=<jobstatus>] [catalog=<catalog>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Shows the table of job status codes from the catalog Status table: code letter (T, E, f, ...), description, severity, and exit level and exit status for finished states. Programs use it to explain the one\-letter status of list jobs. It only reads the catalog.
.PP
The filter must be attached to the command word (.jobstatus=T); a separate word is ignored and gives the whole table. catalog= selects a catalog; an unknown name is ignored and the first catalog is used.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.SS "\&.jobstatus"
.TP
.B "\&.jobstatus[=<.jobstatus>]"
One JobStatus letter (text; the value may be left out)
.TP
.B "catalog=<catalog>"
Catalog name (name; values from .catalogs)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "\&.jobstatus"
show all job status codes
.TP
.B "\&.jobstatus=T"
show only the row for code T
.SH ORIGIN
Bareos console command.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR odir\-commands (7),
.BR oconsole (1)
